# Data comparison across units

Verifies mixed-unit comparisons scale the coarser operand to the finer unit before comparing. 1KB equals 1000B exactly, so `==`, `<=`, and `>=` hold while `!=` does not; likewise 1MB is not greater than 1000KB because both magnitudes coincide after scaling.

>>> source
kilo: int = 1KB
thousand: int = 1000B
print(kilo == thousand)
print(kilo != thousand)
print(kilo <= thousand)
print(kilo >= thousand)
mega: int = 1MB
print(mega > 1000KB)
print(mega == 1000KB)

<<< stdout
true
false
true
true
false
true

<<< stderr
